[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-28271"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/assets/7dc806c646f1e9f5edbfef789fbdc9dfca2745c637906bd61eccb8072440e8c0.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to one decimal place, find the area of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={63}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘}) & =\\frac{3x+2}{3x} \\\\ 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘}) & =3x+2 \\\\ 3x\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘})-3x & =2 \\\\ 3x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘})-1) & =2 \\\\ x & =\\frac{2}{3(\\operatorname{tan}⁡({63}^{∘})-1)} \\\\ x & =0.692\\,5…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =3x+2=3(0.692\\,5…)+2=4.077\\,6…, \\\\ AC & =3x=3(0.692\\,5…)=2.077\\,6….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}(2.077\\,6…)(4.077\\,6…) \\\\  & =4.236\\,0… \\\\  & ≈4.2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the one decimal place." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-28319/selection/07e9bc46a40c356826021ebe569407128c0d312bea1fd767b111c727e40d1018" :answer/id #uuid "03fb56c6-13cd-5ec5-9ae0-8ab1ed3349f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "220" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28319/selection/e12f73422a456eca8c83cae70999c506825a539631c33c529fb793c051a91c96" :answer/id #uuid "e003695d-b7f7-5ccb-a094-11c9754522fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "450" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28319/selection/6d5e653a0cc5c6e6fc44c5c3386727c89009586dc5171332dccb4c794ca30987" :answer/id #uuid "aa2d8101-6379-577e-bc22-ee9ef895b0fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "330" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28319/selection/ceeb45a591a9149928d526611589351bf4d69ef474587b1e33a35f64c8a092e4" :answer/id #uuid "f3d80943-ed5b-5ec6-9507-ac6a43992483" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "370" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28319/selection/feccf1d787deaa2db8d6f1c5144663a62c7f847db88780db80f98a131046d01c" :answer/id #uuid "3eb86b9e-d0b7-5dda-9419-dfb0108accaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "250" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-28319/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a9365dd0-5de5-5bb3-943c-7ba77bffe6ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-28319/selection/e12f73422a456eca8c83cae70999c506825a539631c33c529fb793c051a91c96" :answer-field/choices ["q-28319/selection/07e9bc46a40c356826021ebe569407128c0d312bea1fd767b111c727e40d1018" "q-28319/selection/e12f73422a456eca8c83cae70999c506825a539631c33c529fb793c051a91c96" "q-28319/selection/6d5e653a0cc5c6e6fc44c5c3386727c89009586dc5171332dccb4c794ca30987" "q-28319/selection/ceeb45a591a9149928d526611589351bf4d69ef474587b1e33a35f64c8a092e4" "q-28319/selection/feccf1d787deaa2db8d6f1c5144663a62c7f847db88780db80f98a131046d01c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-28319" :question/id #uuid "93d460d7-5e43-5c54-8dd9-9e426b38eacb" :question/math-academy-id "q-28319" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/assets/576323c48b707bb198045ab932342e53709c7a3678282835430e506c1a9dd605.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={45}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({45}^{∘}) & =\\frac{5x+5}{6x} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{5x+5}{6x} \\\\ 6x & =5x+5 \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =6x=6(5)=30, \\\\ BC & =5x+5=5(5)+5=30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 30\\cdot 30 \\\\  & =450.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-28319/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe83dedc-3034-5e3a-b546-dd57c0ccc6e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-28319"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-76770/selection/a59e10e9ca0b8a69d2b8425f1c9930ee0733ea061a1d6430398562813d750649" :answer/id #uuid "d605baf3-7549-52a3-95de-a7fbf0494f48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "120" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76770/selection/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" :answer/id #uuid "65a06be2-84de-5625-a5a8-48a204b0b1b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76770/selection/a2ce0d7121680ad5ca64b109a32cd456c311ade4af21eb0a0dd652e8319117f1" :answer/id #uuid "9e2e8a65-90c6-5a17-9a6b-5c17a7b80204" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "80" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76770/selection/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" :answer/id #uuid "de20898a-7e94-5aa2-9055-879af1c652f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76770/selection/e8fca892866a06a1ab302627b9de911942e4dfff7666b327843df0729f3939b1" :answer/id #uuid "c96e4c66-bcf7-592f-9473-d891842bfccd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "105" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-76770/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b0216c88-f52e-57a7-bbe9-c8632f3d014c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-76770/selection/a2ce0d7121680ad5ca64b109a32cd456c311ade4af21eb0a0dd652e8319117f1" :answer-field/choices ["q-76770/selection/a59e10e9ca0b8a69d2b8425f1c9930ee0733ea061a1d6430398562813d750649" "q-76770/selection/23a7b929cccc5bdeb88db3bdc770afbaf59570d63e930fc5c94f26cb6f5091dc" "q-76770/selection/a2ce0d7121680ad5ca64b109a32cd456c311ade4af21eb0a0dd652e8319117f1" "q-76770/selection/ca566c3861ad95266b92d3d8e36c85c39daf1d1780cc1bf826ae0ac7accce583" "q-76770/selection/e8fca892866a06a1ab302627b9de911942e4dfff7666b327843df0729f3939b1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-76770" :question/id #uuid "1d010a52-cb85-50be-9c14-2be3fabea947" :question/math-academy-id "q-76770" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/assets/f1880dc62f774152ce5076a313928c0e8109ca174184704c5880891ed9243718.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{2}{5},$ calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{2}{5}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} & =\\frac{2x+4}{6x+8} \\\\ 2(6x+8) & =5(2x+4) \\\\ 12x+16 & =10x+20 \\\\ 12x-10x & =20-16 \\\\ 2x & =4 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2x+4=2(2)+4=8, \\\\ AC & =6x+8=6(2)+8=20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 20\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =80.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-76770/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51739685-2d53-5c9b-870b-b557ffdf2768"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-76770"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-251084/field-1/8781b1aee770a8ec5ac8240cc6c17b8b1ed577974949c5e71bedbbd52d671e84" :answer/id #uuid "92b53a1d-6bea-5b5e-9866-21ac6b088d73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "361" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251084/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "a370bfe0-43a2-5f72-bec9-1f4acd4d3b61" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251084/field-1/8781b1aee770a8ec5ac8240cc6c17b8b1ed577974949c5e71bedbbd52d671e84" :answer-field/choices ["q-251084/field-1/8781b1aee770a8ec5ac8240cc6c17b8b1ed577974949c5e71bedbbd52d671e84"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251084" :question/id #uuid "2cd6b918-cdfb-5e98-9708-c8e5cdeb5894" :question/math-academy-id "q-251084" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/assets/4572bd2ef8f6086ed80f5ac21e045e3cf2359680872a958a40d2f1e72f22d980.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=2,$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=2.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{9x+2}{5x-1} \\\\ 2(5x-1) & =9x+2 \\\\ 10x-2 & =9x+2 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =9x+2=9(4)+2=38, \\\\ AC & =5x-1=5(4)-1=19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 38\\cdot 19 \\\\  & =361.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-251084/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51739685-2d53-5c9b-870b-b557ffdf2768"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-251084"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-251127/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer/id #uuid "a33beaa4-824b-5dba-b98a-336924823fa6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "30" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-251127/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "65c19cd5-250d-5655-8297-513ad904b4fb" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-251127/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8" :answer-field/choices ["q-251127/field-1/a4c8bdda186d0d425e9963bf17967cd5e356d934f319fa58135b8f8cf8a589f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-251127" :question/id #uuid "cc11a7a5-2ec3-59ea-b94f-5fb360c962b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-251127" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13987450/assets/ba89c2cf139dd6251804ed0758c4edc4690463ba5ae14867549881a29736f9e6.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{12}{13},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{12}{13},$ where $\\theta =m∠B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ adjacent to $∠B.$ Hence, we can use the cosine ratio to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{12}{13} & =\\frac{12}{AB} \\\\ AB & =\\frac{12}{12}\\cdot 13 \\\\ AB & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the missing side $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}-B{C}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{13}^{2}-{12}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{169-144} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-251127/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "437a71fe-92e0-58e3-9f49-6560b2755776"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-251127"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
